  "body": "This was most recently raised to the WebGPU group in https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/discussions/3634.\r\nThe desire (I believe) is for an API to find out e.g. when an update to a [page? element?] actually \"hits the screen\". It can be useful to find out these latencies (or at least useful predictions thereof), as detailed more in that WebGPU discussion.\r\n\r\nI believe this is more of an HTML spec thing though, rather than WebGPU. Specifically, this feels like something akin to requestAnimationFrame or requestVideoFrameCallback, or maybe other APIs I'm not familiar with.\r\n\r\nI'm wondering what you think!",
